**Problem.** `::item` resolves its argument as a number or as the gameval `obj.<arg>`. Anything else throws "Missing mapping" from `asRSCM` instead of replying, e.g. `::item saw`: the saw's gameval is `obj.poh_saw`.

**Change.** `resolveObj` looks the gameval up with `RSCM.getRSCMOrNull`. With no gameval, it falls back to the lowest-id unnoted, non-placeholder obj whose cache name matches (case-insensitive, underscores read as spaces). A name that matches nothing returns null, so the command gives its existing "There is no obj mapped to: '...'" reply.

**Tests.** None added (admin command). Checked in game on our build: `::item saw` spawns a Saw.

**Caveats.** When several objs share a name, the lowest id wins (usually the base item).

**Release note.** `::item` accepts an item's in-game name when it isn't a gameval name, and no longer throws on unknown names.

**Checklist**
- [x] The change compiles (`./gradlew build`).
- [x] Tests related to the change pass (`./gradlew assemble test integration`, `spotlessCheck`).
- [x] No documentation change needed.
- [x] No unrelated formatting or dependency changes.
- [x] Manual testing notes are under Tests above.
